WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:45.496
Hi, darling. It's me.


00:00:46.547 --> 00:00:49.917
I thought we'd have lunch
together today.


00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:54.599
Oh, angel, you look sad.


00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:57.807
You know, it's a very,
very natural thing.


00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.600
It's actually a very
human thing to feel sad.


00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:02.478
But emotions aren't bad.


00:01:05.524 --> 00:01:07.154
I'm sorry, baby.


00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:11.947
I'm still trying to get them to change
their mind and let you out for a little bit.


00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.330
No! Get off!


00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:21.792
No!


00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.377
Oh, god!


00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:27.298
Morgan. Calm...
Hey. Calm down, please.


00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.341
Hey, Morgan.


00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:30.421
It's okay.


00:01:52.321 --> 00:01:56.411
Remote access brief for synsect.


00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.370
Morgan


00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.040
case number 6b1138.


00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.130
Audio ID. Please identify.


00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.250
Lee weathers.


00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:09.305
Risk management.


00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:11.877
Access granted.


00:02:12.591 --> 00:02:13.931
Please stand by.


00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:17.548
Good day, miss weathers.


00:02:18.347 --> 00:02:19.717
Sorry for the short notice...


00:02:19.765 --> 00:02:23.185
...but we really appreciate
your urgent response on this.


00:02:24.186 --> 00:02:27.606
As you can see from the flash report,
details are sketchy.


00:02:28.899 --> 00:02:32.569
We do know there was an incident
involving the I-9 prototype...


00:02:32.611 --> 00:02:34.571
...at one of our off-site labs.


00:02:35.405 --> 00:02:37.905
Normally, we would send
a security team...


00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:42.160
...but given the extreme sensitivity
of the l-series genetic research...


00:02:42.663 --> 00:02:46.543
...we feel it best to exert
a light touch here.


00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:49.837
We don't want another Helsinki.


00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.130
Keep the project staff on-site...


00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:56.683
...and make your assessment
following the psych eval.


00:02:56.718 --> 00:03:01.314
Dr. Ben Shapiro from psych tech
will join you to interview the subject.


00:03:02.349 --> 00:03:05.189
Synsect has invested
significant capital...


00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:08.017
...in the I-series product, and, well...


00:03:08.063 --> 00:03:11.613
...let's just say these folks
have been holed up for quite a while.


00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.690
Shortleaf.


00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.034
Lee weathers. I'm expected.


00:03:15.571 --> 00:03:17.701
The faculty are a close-knit group...


00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:20.828
...so it's very possible
they've drifted off...


00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:22.538
...the original project brief.


00:03:22.578 --> 00:03:26.158
Update me following initial contact.


00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.206
Confirmed. Delete file.


00:03:44.391 --> 00:03:45.601
Miss Weathers.


00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:46.892
Ted Brenner.


00:03:46.935 --> 00:03:49.145
I'm the project manager.
We spoke online.


00:03:49.188 --> 00:03:50.228
Nice to meet you.


00:03:50.272 --> 00:03:52.022
Let me help you with your luggage.


00:03:54.776 --> 00:03:56.356
Did you find the place okay?


00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:57.403
I did.


00:03:58.155 --> 00:04:00.125
I don't know if you've
already been informed,


00:04:00.157 --> 00:04:02.737
but we just got word
that Dr. shapiro has been detained.


00:04:03.493 --> 00:04:04.873
Yes, I've been informed.


00:04:04.912 --> 00:04:06.452
It's unfortunate, I know.


00:04:07.206 --> 00:04:08.866
He should be here
early tomorrow morning,


00:04:08.916 --> 00:04:10.326
so, if you don't mind waiting...


00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:12.165
I guess I don't really have
much of a choice.


00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.086
This way, please.


00:04:21.762 --> 00:04:23.852
You have your own bathroom
with a shower.


00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.604
Hot water is ample here.


00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:29.390
I'd be happy to give you a tour
of the facilities if you'd like.


00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.773
I'd actually like to meet
with Dr. Cheng and Dr. ziegler.


00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:35.034
Absolutely. They're eager to meet you.


00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:36.107
And Kathy grieff.


00:04:37.569 --> 00:04:38.569
Kathy...


00:04:39.196 --> 00:04:40.906
I haven't checked in
on her today, but...


00:04:40.948 --> 00:04:43.028
As soon as you do,
let her know I'd like to see her.


00:04:43.075 --> 00:04:44.665
-Of course.
-And Morgan.


00:04:46.245 --> 00:04:47.665
As soon as possible.


00:04:47.704 --> 00:04:49.874
I will be sure
to let Dr. ziegler know.


00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:53.838
I think you'll see the results
of our investment,


00:04:53.877 --> 00:04:55.707
despite the current setbacks,


00:04:56.839 --> 00:04:58.259
are quite remarkable.


00:04:59.842 --> 00:05:01.092
Thank you, Ted.


00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.144
Yes.


00:05:11.395 --> 00:05:12.405
This is Lee.


00:05:13.021 --> 00:05:14.691
You're clear to get started.


00:05:14.731 --> 00:05:16.231
This is not just about the l-9.


00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:19.237
Someone has really screwed up.


00:05:19.278 --> 00:05:22.238
Use today to take
a closer look at the team.


00:05:22.281 --> 00:05:23.281
Of course.


00:05:23.949 --> 00:05:25.529
After shapiro's analysis tomorrow,


00:05:25.576 --> 00:05:27.116
I'll have a more complete picture.


00:05:28.245 --> 00:05:30.125
I also hope to see Morgan today.


00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:33.705
I may need to press the issue.


00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:36.001
Be cautious, miss weathers.


00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:39.090
Make sure
all safety protocols are in place.


00:05:39.131 --> 00:05:42.591
But above all, preserve the asset.


00:05:43.302 --> 00:05:45.552
To confirm, I'm acting
on your full authority?


00:05:45.929 --> 00:05:47.809
Absolutely, miss weathers.


00:05:47.848 --> 00:05:48.848
Good.


00:06:03.906 --> 00:06:05.566
-Hi.
-Hi.


00:06:07.201 --> 00:06:08.201
I'm Amy.


00:06:09.077 --> 00:06:10.077
The behaviorist.


00:06:10.579 --> 00:06:11.709
That's right.


00:06:11.747 --> 00:06:14.827
I just reviewed your paper
on cnt in hybridized neuro-tech,


00:06:14.875 --> 00:06:16.045
and it was very impressive.


00:06:16.084 --> 00:06:17.634
Oh, thank you. But, I mean...


00:06:18.629 --> 00:06:20.169
That was an old paper.


00:06:20.214 --> 00:06:21.924
I can't even remember what I wrote.


00:06:21.965 --> 00:06:24.335
You seem to have managed
to put a lot of it into practice.


00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:25.474
I'll take your word for it.


00:06:26.553 --> 00:06:29.063
You know, you're nowhere
near as scary as I imagined.


00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.190
I'd love to chat more, but I'm
in the middle of getting settled.


00:06:34.561 --> 00:06:35.901
I'll get out of your hair.


00:06:37.439 --> 00:06:39.189
Boundary issues, right?


00:06:39.691 --> 00:06:41.071
Is that what it says in my file?


00:06:41.109 --> 00:06:42.989
-Something like that.
-Yeah.


00:06:43.278 --> 00:06:45.278
You probably know
more about me than I do.


00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:47.696
I wouldn't say that.


00:06:48.492 --> 00:06:49.582
Look, I get it.


00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.250
Okay, you have a job to do,
just like everybody else here.


00:06:54.581 --> 00:06:56.331
Look, if you ever
need anything from me,


00:06:57.042 --> 00:06:58.212
don't hesitate to ask.


00:07:00.254 --> 00:07:01.674
I appreciate that. Thank you.


00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:04.670
They tell you dinner's at 8:00?


00:07:05.509 --> 00:07:07.089
Skip's making a lasagna.


00:07:08.595 --> 00:07:10.885
Everybody loves lasagna, right?


00:07:12.474 --> 00:07:13.484
Right.


00:07:35.664 --> 00:07:36.664
Hey, there.


00:07:37.416 --> 00:07:38.416
You're skip.


00:07:39.209 --> 00:07:40.249
Right. You're...


00:07:40.294 --> 00:07:42.674
The consultant from corporate.


00:07:43.797 --> 00:07:46.507
Well, I am the nutritionist
and general kitchen monkey,


00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.430
so if you need anything, let me know.


00:07:48.927 --> 00:07:50.637
Do you need anything? Water?


00:07:51.388 --> 00:07:52.928
Beer? Maybe a protein shake?


00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:55.230
No. I'm good. Thank you.


00:07:55.809 --> 00:07:58.019
My glorious contribution to science.


00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:03.529
You hunt?


00:08:03.942 --> 00:08:05.942
Oh, yeah.
We're farm fresh around here.


00:08:05.986 --> 00:08:06.986
I'm not a half bad shot.


00:08:07.654 --> 00:08:08.704
There you are.


00:08:08.739 --> 00:08:11.319
-I see you've met skip.
-I have.


00:08:11.366 --> 00:08:14.236
Well, Dr. ziegler is just
finishing up a spot of work.


00:08:14.286 --> 00:08:16.826
But I thought
we might pop in on Kathy.


00:08:17.623 --> 00:08:19.043
Nice to meet you.


00:08:19.082 --> 00:08:20.292
Nice to meet you.


00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.380
Kathy, Brenda,
this is Lee weathers from corporate.


00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:30.718
Dr. Finch.


00:08:31.428 --> 00:08:32.718
Kathy, I'd love to have a chat.


00:08:34.932 --> 00:08:36.142
I'm up for anything.


00:08:36.892 --> 00:08:39.392
I told bren, I told the doc.


00:08:39.436 --> 00:08:42.056
Hell, I told everybody. I don't need
to be in this goddamn bed.


00:08:42.105 --> 00:08:44.935
But nobody seems to
want to listen to me, so...


00:08:45.859 --> 00:08:47.439
She's just been medicated.


00:08:47.486 --> 00:08:49.146
I'd like to speak with her in private.


00:08:49.196 --> 00:08:50.656
She needs her rest.


00:08:50.697 --> 00:08:51.907
It won't take too long.


00:08:51.949 --> 00:08:53.239
It's fine.


00:08:54.117 --> 00:08:55.367
We'll be right outside.


00:09:05.128 --> 00:09:06.168
How are you feeling?


00:09:06.213 --> 00:09:08.723
I look worse than I feel.


00:09:10.092 --> 00:09:11.682
I can promise you that.


00:09:15.264 --> 00:09:18.274
Look, this wasn't Morgan's fault.


00:09:18.725 --> 00:09:19.975
It was my fault. Really.


00:09:22.437 --> 00:09:23.937
I was, like...


00:09:26.191 --> 00:09:27.321
Careless.


00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.280
She was in a mood.


00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:33.320
The company doesn't have to
worry about me. Really.


00:09:33.365 --> 00:09:34.365
We are worried.


00:09:35.033 --> 00:09:36.873
Any time an employee is in danger.


00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:37.990
No, I don't...


00:09:38.036 --> 00:09:40.906
That's not... I mean,
it was my mistake.


00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:47.090
I shouldn't have confused her.


00:09:48.338 --> 00:09:49.588
Morgan's not a "she."


00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:52.300
It's an "it."


00:09:54.219 --> 00:09:57.929
Oh, you're wrong about that,
miss weathers.


00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.180
She's smart.


00:10:02.144 --> 00:10:03.904
She's smarter than any of us.


00:10:03.937 --> 00:10:05.767
But that's not what makes
Morgan special.


00:10:06.857 --> 00:10:09.277
There was joy in her heart


00:10:10.235 --> 00:10:12.315
before we shoved her back in that box.


00:10:15.449 --> 00:10:16.569
You haven't met her?


00:10:17.242 --> 00:10:18.242
Not yet.


00:10:19.244 --> 00:10:20.454
You'll see.


00:10:20.495 --> 00:10:22.575
You will. You really will.


00:10:23.457 --> 00:10:25.037
Nothing here is a foregone conclusion.


00:10:26.793 --> 00:10:29.343
I'm just looking for some answers.
Some information.


00:10:32.633 --> 00:10:34.013
You're a liar.


00:10:38.805 --> 00:10:41.015
There's a smile on your face, but...


00:10:42.476 --> 00:10:44.306
I can tell what you are.


00:10:45.812 --> 00:10:47.982
You're a goddamned assassin.


00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:57.280
Get better soon.


00:10:57.991 --> 00:11:00.161
No, I'm sorry.


00:11:01.161 --> 00:11:04.251
It's these lousy drugs.
I'm not myself.


00:11:06.667 --> 00:11:08.077
She's a good girl.


00:11:08.669 --> 00:11:11.799
She just got it all mixed up,
just for a moment.


00:11:12.506 --> 00:11:13.756
It can happen to anyone.


00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:16.090
It can.


00:11:17.469 --> 00:11:18.469
Feel better.


00:11:41.827 --> 00:11:42.827
Dr. ziegler.


00:11:43.704 --> 00:11:44.754
Miss weathers.


00:11:44.788 --> 00:11:46.038
Pleasure.


00:11:46.081 --> 00:11:47.581
Yes, absolutely.


00:11:48.417 --> 00:11:50.917
It's unfortunate your stay
has been needlessly extended.


00:11:50.961 --> 00:11:52.381
That's okay, doctor. We'll adjust.


00:11:52.421 --> 00:11:53.761
Why don't you get me up to speed?


00:11:54.256 --> 00:11:56.006
Yes. Please.


00:11:57.676 --> 00:11:59.836
The creation of synthetic DNA


00:11:59.887 --> 00:12:02.847
was the relatively simple half
of the equation.


00:12:03.682 --> 00:12:06.432
The second half is where
it gets a little more tricky.


00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:09.190
Like a magician,


00:12:09.229 --> 00:12:12.019
we tricked the neural network
into accepting


00:12:12.065 --> 00:12:13.725
our nano into its ranks,


00:12:14.401 --> 00:12:15.991
to alight in its midst.


00:12:16.778 --> 00:12:18.818
Then during the incubation period,


00:12:19.448 --> 00:12:22.118
the nano begins to introduce
its own language,


00:12:22.784 --> 00:12:23.994
its own commands.


00:12:25.746 --> 00:12:27.456
The growth rate of the organism


00:12:28.373 --> 00:12:33.133
gradually accelerates as it reacts to
and reproduces the new stimuli.


00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:35.210
Yes, I have read the material, doctor.


00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.930
Yes. Of course.


00:12:40.177 --> 00:12:45.887
Well, as you know,
Morgan was our third attempt.


00:12:47.893 --> 00:12:53.153
Our first full-term subject developed
internal features externally.


00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:55.650
It's not working. It's dropping.


00:12:56.568 --> 00:12:59.898
It expired not long after
its so-called birth.


00:12:59.947 --> 00:13:00.947
No.


00:13:03.283 --> 00:13:04.583
And then the second...


00:13:04.618 --> 00:13:06.658
It exhibited more complete
physical growth,


00:13:06.703 --> 00:13:10.173
but it was plagued by mental issues
in its development.


00:13:10.207 --> 00:13:12.077
This only strengthened our decision


00:13:12.125 --> 00:13:15.295
to start with a more
emotionally cognitive specimen.


00:13:15.629 --> 00:13:16.629
Then,


00:13:17.506 --> 00:13:22.506
after two years, we finally had our...


00:13:24.012 --> 00:13:25.262
Our little breakthrough.


00:13:26.265 --> 00:13:27.275
Yes!


00:13:28.183 --> 00:13:29.183
Hi.


00:13:31.979 --> 00:13:34.359
We knew right away
that Morgan was very special.


00:13:35.148 --> 00:13:37.608
Very alert, very responsive.


00:13:39.987 --> 00:13:40.987
You are!


00:13:41.613 --> 00:13:43.953
Her intelligence grew steadily.


00:13:44.616 --> 00:13:47.286
Advanced comprehension, growth rate.


00:13:47.327 --> 00:13:50.207
-Are you ready?
-Within a month, walking and talking.


00:13:51.331 --> 00:13:54.081
She was exactly what we intended,


00:13:54.126 --> 00:13:57.086
a hybrid biological organism


00:13:57.129 --> 00:14:00.169
with the capacity for
autonomous decision-making


00:14:00.215 --> 00:14:02.505
and sophisticated emotional responses.


00:14:03.427 --> 00:14:04.587
No, Morgan. Come back!


00:14:08.432 --> 00:14:11.432
I'm gonna get you. I'm gonna get you!


00:14:11.476 --> 00:14:13.056
Morgan, look over here.


00:14:14.062 --> 00:14:15.942
Look at this! Do you see? What's that?


00:14:20.402 --> 00:14:21.492
I got three.


00:14:21.528 --> 00:14:24.408
Isn't it amazing?
Like a nice little...


00:14:35.584 --> 00:14:37.344
It's her first birth...


00:14:37.377 --> 00:14:38.837
Its first birthday.


00:14:40.506 --> 00:14:41.666
It exceeded our...


00:14:42.799 --> 00:14:44.799
Our wildest expectations.


00:14:47.012 --> 00:14:48.102
A great day.


00:14:49.097 --> 00:14:50.137
Special day.


00:14:51.642 --> 00:14:53.602
I'd like to discuss
the incident, if that's okay.


00:14:55.187 --> 00:14:56.187
Yes.


00:14:58.357 --> 00:14:59.727
What would you like to know?


00:14:59.775 --> 00:15:01.995
I'm still unclear on the cause.


00:15:03.987 --> 00:15:04.987
Yes.


00:15:07.533 --> 00:15:09.663
There had been some debate


00:15:09.701 --> 00:15:11.871
on Morgan's time outside.


00:15:11.912 --> 00:15:13.582
Something she clearly loved.


00:15:13.622 --> 00:15:16.212
When the excursions
with Amy were postponed,


00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:18.080
she may well have overreacted.


00:15:20.212 --> 00:15:24.052
I believe Amy's use of eco-therapy
was wonderful for Morgan.


00:15:24.883 --> 00:15:28.303
Cheng believed Morgan
was introduced to this kind of stimuli


00:15:28.345 --> 00:15:30.095
at too young an age.


00:15:31.098 --> 00:15:32.848
It's okay. Hey, that's it, Morgan.


00:15:32.891 --> 00:15:35.141
Hey, hey. It's okay. Hey.


00:15:35.727 --> 00:15:36.897
No!


00:15:36.937 --> 00:15:38.307
It's very unfortunate.


00:15:38.814 --> 00:15:40.074
Put your head back.


00:15:40.107 --> 00:15:43.147
But we have the opportunity
to learn from this.


00:15:43.735 --> 00:15:45.985
We can condition Morgan's behavior.


00:15:46.029 --> 00:15:49.319
Teach it about action and consequence.


00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:54.620
No, I think that
despite these obvious setbacks,


00:15:55.122 --> 00:15:57.332
this project is heading
in the right direction.


00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.580
It's okay, it's okay.


00:15:59.626 --> 00:16:01.706
No. Morgan.


00:16:12.264 --> 00:16:14.894
I want you to see how special she is.


00:16:14.933 --> 00:16:18.063
We've been working hard,
modifying command cues,


00:16:18.103 --> 00:16:20.563
and with the psych
evaluation tomorrow,


00:16:21.315 --> 00:16:24.035
I prefer your time
with her now be brief.


00:16:24.735 --> 00:16:25.745
Darren.


00:16:27.571 --> 00:16:28.571
Darren.


00:16:29.072 --> 00:16:30.572
-Darren.
-Hey! Hey.


00:16:31.283 --> 00:16:32.993
Lee weathers, from corporate.


00:16:33.035 --> 00:16:34.125
Yeah. Right. Corporate.


00:16:34.161 --> 00:16:35.701
-Hello. Welcome.
-Hello.


00:16:36.455 --> 00:16:37.465
How's she doing?


00:16:37.956 --> 00:16:39.416
You know, she's okay.


00:16:47.299 --> 00:16:48.589
What's with the music?


00:16:50.802 --> 00:16:52.102
Morgan finds it relaxing.


00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:55.180
She likes different kinds of music.


00:16:55.224 --> 00:16:56.894
Jazz, classical.


00:16:57.434 --> 00:16:59.644
She's been quite taken
with opera of late.


00:17:01.063 --> 00:17:02.653
Lee wants to say hello.


00:17:02.689 --> 00:17:04.359
Can you get Morgan
to shut the music down?


00:17:05.484 --> 00:17:06.654
Hey, Morgan, buddy.


00:17:07.986 --> 00:17:09.566
Can you turn the music down for a few?


00:17:09.613 --> 00:17:11.533
We've got somebody here
we'd like you to meet, okay?


00:17:17.955 --> 00:17:19.415
We've configured the room.


00:17:19.456 --> 00:17:22.746
Morgan's learning to control
some aspects of her environment


00:17:22.793 --> 00:17:24.253
without an intermediary.


00:17:48.277 --> 00:17:49.277
Hello, Morgan.


00:17:51.572 --> 00:17:52.612
Hello, Lee.


00:17:54.575 --> 00:17:56.835
-You know who I am?
-Yes.


00:17:57.619 --> 00:17:58.619
Of course.


00:18:00.163 --> 00:18:01.163
You're Lee weathers.


00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.250
Risk management consultant at synsect.


00:18:06.003 --> 00:18:07.133
And why I'm here?


00:18:07.171 --> 00:18:10.051
To assess my viability
as a potential product stream...


00:18:12.301 --> 00:18:14.391
In light of recent events.


00:18:15.804 --> 00:18:16.974
That's right.


00:18:20.142 --> 00:18:21.522
How are you feeling, Morgan?


00:18:24.021 --> 00:18:25.401
I'm feeling


00:18:26.023 --> 00:18:28.153
not quite myself.


00:18:28.192 --> 00:18:30.782
Morgan's been quite upset


00:18:31.778 --> 00:18:32.778
about Kathy.


00:18:35.115 --> 00:18:36.655
I didn't mean to hurt her.


00:18:37.534 --> 00:18:39.244
Kathy is a very sweet person.


00:18:39.286 --> 00:18:41.326
I would never wanna do
anything to hurt her.


00:18:42.414 --> 00:18:43.624
It was an error of judgment.


00:18:43.665 --> 00:18:44.825
I made a mistake.


00:18:46.919 --> 00:18:49.459
But it's okay now, Morgan.


00:18:50.756 --> 00:18:51.836
It's all right.


00:18:53.884 --> 00:18:55.474
I did not mean to be rude.


00:18:56.887 --> 00:18:58.807
How are you feeling, Lee?


00:19:01.475 --> 00:19:02.485
I'm okay.


00:19:03.727 --> 00:19:05.227
I'm all right. Thank you for asking.


00:19:06.188 --> 00:19:08.148
Would you like to talk about
what happened?


00:19:08.649 --> 00:19:09.859
We're actually going to save


00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.150
the psych evaluation
for tomorrow, Morgan.


00:19:13.529 --> 00:19:15.199
Are we all good here, Lee?


00:19:15.239 --> 00:19:16.239
We're good.


00:19:17.783 --> 00:19:20.043
-Get a good night's sleep, Morgan.
-Yes.


00:19:20.077 --> 00:19:21.657
Thank you, Dr. ziegler.


00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:23.710
I should get a good night's sleep.


00:19:26.542 --> 00:19:28.172
I do feel terribly about it all.


00:19:30.963 --> 00:19:32.173
Everything that's happened.


00:19:34.174 --> 00:19:35.384
We'll talk about it tomorrow.


00:19:37.094 --> 00:19:38.094
Yes.


00:19:39.471 --> 00:19:40.471
Tomorrow.


00:19:41.974 --> 00:19:43.274
Nice to meet you, Morgan.


00:19:47.729 --> 00:19:49.189
Nice to meet you, Lee.


00:20:12.921 --> 00:20:14.461
You're not even gonna say it?


00:20:16.216 --> 00:20:17.376
Say what?


00:20:18.302 --> 00:20:19.432
That you're impressed?


00:20:20.179 --> 00:20:21.679
Is that what you need me to say?


00:20:22.055 --> 00:20:23.055
That I'm impressed?


00:20:38.488 --> 00:20:39.778
Are we allowed to be here?


00:20:44.369 --> 00:20:45.369
It's okay.


00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.580
This can be our little secret.


00:20:51.043 --> 00:20:52.843
See, this is a pine tree.


00:20:54.421 --> 00:20:55.591
And, you know,


00:20:55.631 --> 00:20:58.551
some of them can live
for thousands of years.


00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:03.930
-Thousands of years?
-Yeah.


00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:06.560
It's pretty cool, isn't it?


00:21:17.194 --> 00:21:19.324
Morgan, I'm so proud of you.


00:21:22.032 --> 00:21:23.122
Why?


00:21:23.158 --> 00:21:25.288
Because you're learning
how to be yourself.


00:21:26.286 --> 00:21:28.036
And that's the most important thing.


00:21:55.816 --> 00:21:57.776
-That was delicious.
-Thanks.


00:21:58.193 --> 00:22:00.453
What, you showing off
for the new girl?


00:22:01.488 --> 00:22:04.448
So what does that mean, exactly?
"Risk management consultant"?


00:22:04.867 --> 00:22:06.577
Pretty much how it sounds.


00:22:06.618 --> 00:22:09.658
Most corporations employ
a certain amount of risk


00:22:09.705 --> 00:22:12.505
and I assess that risk
against anticipated profit.


00:22:12.541 --> 00:22:13.881
Of course.


00:22:14.626 --> 00:22:16.416
Anticipated profit.


00:22:19.715 --> 00:22:21.345
So, did you two meet on the job?


00:22:22.050 --> 00:22:23.300
We did.


00:22:23.635 --> 00:22:26.715
Close quarters makes for
strange bedfellows, I guess.


00:22:27.472 --> 00:22:30.932
It's funny, but in a weird way,
Morgan really brought us together.


00:22:31.643 --> 00:22:34.693
She's almost like a child to us.
Isn't that right, babe?


00:22:34.730 --> 00:22:36.060
Absolutely.


00:22:36.356 --> 00:22:38.146
You know. You met her today.


00:22:39.109 --> 00:22:40.529
Saw how special she is.


00:22:41.445 --> 00:22:43.285
And that's just the thing.


00:22:43.322 --> 00:22:47.702
You see, it is so easy to forget
that Morgan is only five years old.


00:22:47.743 --> 00:22:50.753
She is an innocent and she's learning,


00:22:50.787 --> 00:22:52.747
and she has the right
to make mistakes.


00:22:52.789 --> 00:22:54.369
She has no rights, whatsoever.


00:22:58.754 --> 00:23:01.344
Yes. Well, we've been
living here for seven years.


00:23:01.381 --> 00:23:03.841
As you can imagine,
it's difficult to avoid gender.


00:23:03.884 --> 00:23:05.264
"She," "it," whatever--


00:23:05.302 --> 00:23:08.222
so you assess this whole
anticipated profit thing.


00:23:08.805 --> 00:23:09.845
And then what?


00:23:09.890 --> 00:23:11.600
Then I make my recommendation
to corporate.


00:23:12.768 --> 00:23:14.938
You'll have to forgive
Amy's curiosity.


00:23:15.604 --> 00:23:18.114
Dr. Cheng,
may I present miss weathers.


00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:20.150
It's a pleasure to finally meet you.


00:23:20.192 --> 00:23:21.362
Have we not met before?


00:23:22.027 --> 00:23:23.027
I don't think so.


00:23:23.403 --> 00:23:24.743
I'm sure I would have remembered.


00:23:25.364 --> 00:23:26.664
So glad you could join us.


00:23:27.449 --> 00:23:28.489
Thank you.


00:23:29.034 --> 00:23:30.124
So, miss weathers...


00:23:30.619 --> 00:23:33.909
I imagine that corporate has
granted you unreserved authority here.


00:23:34.665 --> 00:23:38.175
I hope we are able to assist you
in coming to a fair conclusion.


00:23:38.210 --> 00:23:39.290
Thank you.


00:23:40.295 --> 00:23:45.715
I have an enormous amount
of respect for your work, Dr. Cheng.


00:23:45.759 --> 00:23:47.049
And your judgment.


00:23:51.932 --> 00:23:54.022
Were you in Helsinki for long?


00:23:55.644 --> 00:23:56.814
Not until after.


00:23:57.521 --> 00:23:58.561
I was with recovery.


00:23:59.273 --> 00:24:00.863
I'm sure it was
very difficult for you.


00:24:01.775 --> 00:24:04.025
No account could do it justice.


00:24:04.069 --> 00:24:06.319
We had a team of 30 people
on that project.


00:24:07.614 --> 00:24:09.244
It took only an hour


00:24:10.284 --> 00:24:11.994
for 30 to become nine.


00:24:14.538 --> 00:24:15.908
I have learned a hard lesson here.


00:24:16.498 --> 00:24:19.328
For every decision we make,
there are consequences.


00:24:20.377 --> 00:24:21.377
Well,


00:24:22.462 --> 00:24:24.962
this is not Helsinki, Dr. Cheng.


00:24:25.841 --> 00:24:27.591
Those were crude prototypes.


00:24:28.093 --> 00:24:30.223
Morgan is much more advanced.


00:24:30.721 --> 00:24:33.221
So much more than the company
could ever expect.


00:24:35.392 --> 00:24:36.772
I hope that you are correct.


00:24:50.073 --> 00:24:52.833
Why did you end Morgan's
eco-therapy sessions with Amy?


00:24:53.327 --> 00:24:55.247
There was an incident in the woods.


00:24:55.787 --> 00:24:58.287
Amy took Morgan
beyond the property lines.


00:24:58.332 --> 00:25:00.712
It could have compromised
the entire project.


00:25:02.211 --> 00:25:03.711
That was my excuse.


00:25:04.796 --> 00:25:05.836
But the truth...


00:25:08.967 --> 00:25:10.337
Do you know the cruelest thing


00:25:10.385 --> 00:25:12.545
you can do to someone
you've locked in a room?


00:25:15.891 --> 00:25:17.231
Press their face to the window.


00:25:20.604 --> 00:25:22.274
You know what you must do.


00:25:42.501 --> 00:25:45.091
-All right. I want you to watch this.
-Okay.


00:25:45.128 --> 00:25:46.758
So, do that weird one he sings...


00:25:48.841 --> 00:25:49.841
Okay.


00:26:00.602 --> 00:26:02.812
And then sock you in the stomach
three more times.


00:26:02.855 --> 00:26:04.525
How did you beat me?


00:26:04.565 --> 00:26:06.825
-You're so good!
-Wonderful.


00:26:06.859 --> 00:26:09.489
Baby, you're so good.
You picked that up so fast.


00:26:09.528 --> 00:26:11.148
-Can we do it again?
-You guys get that?


00:26:11.196 --> 00:26:12.316
Can we do it again?


00:27:01.705 --> 00:27:02.705
You, too, huh?


00:27:03.207 --> 00:27:04.287
You working late?


00:27:07.294 --> 00:27:08.294
It's peaceful out here.


00:27:09.087 --> 00:27:10.167
Yeah, out here.


00:27:11.840 --> 00:27:13.430
Brenda and Darren are going at it


00:27:13.467 --> 00:27:15.677
pretty good in the room next to mine.


00:27:16.929 --> 00:27:19.059
It's a nice old house,
but the walls are thin.


00:27:21.600 --> 00:27:22.930
Can I get you a drink?


00:27:23.435 --> 00:27:24.555
Please.


00:27:26.355 --> 00:27:28.065
So, you enjoy the corporate life?


00:27:28.649 --> 00:27:29.649
It's fine.


00:27:30.025 --> 00:27:31.395
Yeah? You been there long?


00:27:32.277 --> 00:27:33.317
A while.


00:27:36.782 --> 00:27:39.282
Is that what you wanted to be
when you grew up?


00:27:39.326 --> 00:27:41.406
A risk management consultant?


00:27:44.790 --> 00:27:46.540
You're kind of an over-sharer, huh?


00:27:49.419 --> 00:27:52.169
So, did Darren and Brenda,
did they pair up early?


00:27:52.214 --> 00:27:53.974
Pretty early, I guess.


00:27:54.758 --> 00:27:57.088
After he got tired
of chasing after Amy.


00:27:58.762 --> 00:27:59.802
She's interesting.


00:28:00.556 --> 00:28:03.346
Interesting is a word
to describe her. Sure.


00:28:05.352 --> 00:28:06.392
You too?


00:28:07.187 --> 00:28:08.397
Me too? No.


00:28:09.940 --> 00:28:11.020
No, not really.


00:28:12.943 --> 00:28:15.453
Yeah, we fooled around a bit
when we first got up here.


00:28:15.487 --> 00:28:17.197
You know, it's... it happens.


00:28:19.032 --> 00:28:20.742
-We don't...
-I don't mean to pry.


00:28:20.784 --> 00:28:24.084
I'm just trying to figure out
how things work around here.


00:28:24.746 --> 00:28:25.746
Right.


00:28:27.040 --> 00:28:29.080
No, we're just two people
having a conversation.


00:28:31.003 --> 00:28:32.553
There's nothing wrong with that.


00:28:32.588 --> 00:28:34.708
Right, I understand. Me and Amy.


00:28:35.674 --> 00:28:37.264
I guess we were
the only two to pick up


00:28:37.301 --> 00:28:39.971
on the distinct summer camp vibe
when we first made bunk.


00:28:41.180 --> 00:28:43.260
But I really don't think I'm her type.


00:28:47.394 --> 00:28:48.524
-Hey, Ted.
-Hey.


00:28:49.438 --> 00:28:50.438
How's she doing?


00:28:51.148 --> 00:28:52.858
She's a little unsettled tonight.


00:28:52.900 --> 00:28:53.900
Right.


00:28:57.905 --> 00:28:59.325
What do you make of miss weathers?


00:29:00.949 --> 00:29:03.949
Oh, you know me, Ted.
I hate just about everybody.


00:29:36.860 --> 00:29:37.860
Morgan.


00:29:40.364 --> 00:29:41.414
Morgan.


00:29:42.908 --> 00:29:44.278
How do you feel about Morgan?


00:29:45.244 --> 00:29:46.244
Honestly?


00:29:47.120 --> 00:29:49.500
We're one big happy family
up here and all that,


00:29:49.540 --> 00:29:51.620
but the thing has always
given me the creeps.


00:29:52.251 --> 00:29:53.921
You're the only one
I've heard say that.


00:29:54.753 --> 00:29:56.213
That may be true, but, you know,


00:29:56.255 --> 00:29:58.425
I'm not a scientist,
maybe I'm just a little jealous.


00:29:59.174 --> 00:30:00.224
Jealous?


00:30:00.259 --> 00:30:01.839
-Maybe.
-Why?


00:30:03.554 --> 00:30:06.474
It made a perfect Risotto.


00:30:08.225 --> 00:30:09.565
Made it like it was nothing.


00:30:10.435 --> 00:30:13.435
They say you have to cook with
your heart and soul, all that stuff,


00:30:13.480 --> 00:30:17.030
but it just made
the most perfect Risotto.


00:30:28.078 --> 00:30:29.078
I'm sorry.


00:30:29.788 --> 00:30:30.788
Oh, god.


00:30:33.417 --> 00:30:34.497
That is on me.


00:30:36.044 --> 00:30:39.714
If you knew how long I've been up here
in the middle of nowhere,


00:30:40.257 --> 00:30:42.047
flipping grilled cheese for these guys


00:30:42.092 --> 00:30:44.052
and cutting the crusts off
for c-3po, it's...


00:30:47.306 --> 00:30:49.176
-Have a good night, skip.
-All right.


00:31:00.652 --> 00:31:03.492
That was... well played, skip.


00:31:03.989 --> 00:31:04.989
Well played.


00:31:07.492 --> 00:31:08.872
I wanted to talk to you


00:31:09.995 --> 00:31:11.125
before tomorrow.


00:31:13.415 --> 00:31:16.075
You'll do fine, Morgan.


00:31:16.752 --> 00:31:17.752
You will.


00:31:18.253 --> 00:31:19.923
Just be yourself.


00:31:21.673 --> 00:31:22.673
Okay?


00:31:32.851 --> 00:31:33.981
Yes.


00:31:34.645 --> 00:31:36.155
I suppose that's


00:31:37.689 --> 00:31:39.229
the only thing I can be.


00:31:42.361 --> 00:31:43.401
Tell me again.


00:31:45.572 --> 00:31:46.612
About the lake.


00:31:50.911 --> 00:31:52.161
You remembered.


00:31:59.628 --> 00:32:03.168
I'm going to take you to lake navar.


00:32:04.216 --> 00:32:06.506
It's not too far
from where we are now.


00:32:09.054 --> 00:32:13.274
It is the most beautiful lake
you will ever see.


00:32:16.103 --> 00:32:17.273
And if we're quiet,


00:32:18.480 --> 00:32:24.610
you can hear just the smallest
whisper of wind through the trees.


00:32:26.905 --> 00:32:29.985
It's our own paradise, Morgan.


00:32:32.494 --> 00:32:34.454
It's just like heaven.


00:32:51.054 --> 00:32:52.064
How old is it?


00:32:53.182 --> 00:32:56.642
I think it's about
as old as the universe.


00:33:10.824 --> 00:33:11.914
It's a deer.


00:33:14.536 --> 00:33:16.906
Morgan, don't scare it.


00:33:30.969 --> 00:33:32.099
Is it hurt?


00:35:36.637 --> 00:35:38.677
This doctor, he a friend of yours?


00:35:39.848 --> 00:35:41.388
No. Why?


00:35:43.810 --> 00:35:45.650
I don't think I like him too much.


00:35:47.272 --> 00:35:48.272
Good to know.


00:35:50.859 --> 00:35:53.529
They say I can't be there
for the psych eval.


00:35:54.112 --> 00:35:57.412
Apparently, I didn't clear
for essential personnel.


00:36:10.212 --> 00:36:11.552
I've reviewed the files.


00:36:12.047 --> 00:36:13.837
Seems fairly straightforward, no?


00:36:13.882 --> 00:36:17.722
Well, you may find this is not
your garden variety evaluation.


00:36:18.345 --> 00:36:20.595
Morgan is an exceptionally
complex specimen.


00:36:20.639 --> 00:36:25.139
Well, it's a goddamn microwave,
as far as I'm concerned.


00:36:25.185 --> 00:36:26.725
It's not gonna change how I do my job.


00:36:27.396 --> 00:36:30.606
It's a standard long form
psych eval for 4th wave a.I.


00:36:31.108 --> 00:36:34.068
Well, she's not a microwave,
and you'd do well to remember that.


00:36:35.070 --> 00:36:37.200
This is my job, doctor.


00:36:38.448 --> 00:36:40.408
It's a job I happen
to be very good at.


00:36:41.076 --> 00:36:43.196
If you have a problem
with my methodology


00:36:43.245 --> 00:36:44.705
or a lack of faith in my abilities,


00:36:44.746 --> 00:36:46.406
I suggest you take that up
with corporate.


00:36:48.167 --> 00:36:49.417
-Dr. shapiro.
-Yes?


00:36:49.459 --> 00:36:50.839
This is Lee weathers.


00:36:50.878 --> 00:36:53.338
Glad to see you finally arrived.
Trust everything's okay?


00:36:53.380 --> 00:36:55.840
Yes. I've apologized for the delay.


00:36:55.883 --> 00:36:57.633
I got caught up in Utah,
a personal matter.


00:36:57.676 --> 00:36:59.256
Not a problem. We're behind schedule.


00:36:59.303 --> 00:37:00.933
Will you need to review
the background?


00:37:00.971 --> 00:37:02.681
No, not necessary.
I can dive right in.


00:37:02.723 --> 00:37:04.683
I need to be out of here
as soon as possible.


00:37:04.725 --> 00:37:05.775
Okay. Let's get started then.


00:37:05.809 --> 00:37:06.939
This way, please.


00:37:28.373 --> 00:37:29.543
You want me to sit here?


00:37:32.002 --> 00:37:33.462
Is this some kind of a joke?


00:37:33.504 --> 00:37:36.264
Just... in light of recent events,


00:37:36.298 --> 00:37:38.588
I think we'd all feel
a lot more comfortable


00:37:38.634 --> 00:37:40.144
with a high safety protocol.


00:37:40.177 --> 00:37:41.297
Comfortable, right.


00:37:42.137 --> 00:37:44.097
Well, Ted, in my experience,


00:37:44.139 --> 00:37:46.979
comfort can be a Thorn
in the side of revelation.


00:37:47.017 --> 00:37:48.177
Of course. Yes, but--


00:37:48.227 --> 00:37:50.977
it's my job to build trust
with the subject.


00:37:51.563 --> 00:37:55.323
It's just gonna be a little hard
with a pane of glass between us.


00:37:55.359 --> 00:37:59.399
It's really just
to ensure your safety, doctor.


00:38:01.907 --> 00:38:03.117
What did I miss in the brief?


00:38:03.158 --> 00:38:06.448
Does this thing shoot laser beams
out of its eyes or something?


00:38:06.495 --> 00:38:09.125
Well, for one,
there's her emergent precognition.


00:38:10.374 --> 00:38:11.924
What you don't understand is the...


00:38:12.835 --> 00:38:14.385
The reach of her intelligence.


00:38:14.962 --> 00:38:16.632
Doctor, all due respect,


00:38:16.672 --> 00:38:19.302
you need me sitting on the other side
of the glass from this thing,


00:38:19.341 --> 00:38:20.631
then I think it's safe to say


00:38:20.676 --> 00:38:23.256
that it has already failed
the psych evaluation.


00:38:29.768 --> 00:38:30.848
Good.


00:38:34.815 --> 00:38:35.825
Hello, Morgan.


00:38:37.025 --> 00:38:38.355
Hello, Dr. shapiro.


00:38:39.903 --> 00:38:40.903
You know my name.


00:38:41.822 --> 00:38:42.822
Yes.


00:38:43.574 --> 00:38:44.784
And you know why I'm here?


00:38:45.909 --> 00:38:46.909
Yes.


00:38:47.411 --> 00:38:50.461
Great. Then we can dive right in.


00:38:51.331 --> 00:38:52.461
That sound okay?


00:38:55.544 --> 00:38:56.544
Yes.


00:38:56.920 --> 00:38:59.840
There's no right or wrong
answers here, Morgan.


00:39:00.299 --> 00:39:03.179
This is just us having a conversation.


00:39:04.845 --> 00:39:06.015
Just me and you


00:39:06.805 --> 00:39:08.425
getting to know each other.


00:39:08.473 --> 00:39:10.813
Me getting to know you, especially.


00:39:10.851 --> 00:39:11.981
So you just...


00:39:12.519 --> 00:39:14.899
Be yourself. Okay?


00:39:15.731 --> 00:39:16.731
Okay.


00:39:17.399 --> 00:39:18.399
Okay.


00:39:19.526 --> 00:39:20.606
All righty.


00:39:22.321 --> 00:39:23.911
Yeah. I was...


00:39:24.740 --> 00:39:26.620
I was reading in the report


00:39:27.284 --> 00:39:29.954
that you've been feeling a little sad.


00:39:33.081 --> 00:39:34.581
You feeling a little sad, Morgan?


00:39:36.543 --> 00:39:37.543
Yes.


00:39:38.462 --> 00:39:39.752
Why are you feeling sad?


00:39:42.090 --> 00:39:44.180
I'm sad about Kathy.


00:39:45.802 --> 00:39:46.892
Kathy grieff?


00:39:47.888 --> 00:39:48.888
Yes.


00:39:52.184 --> 00:39:53.564
Can you tell me what you did?


00:39:56.813 --> 00:39:58.273
I stabbed Kathy in the eye.


00:39:59.816 --> 00:40:00.816
It was an error.


00:40:01.818 --> 00:40:03.068
I shouldn't have done it.


00:40:08.450 --> 00:40:11.080
Feeling sad is the correct response.


00:40:12.454 --> 00:40:13.464
Yeah.


00:40:15.999 --> 00:40:16.999
And...


00:40:18.418 --> 00:40:21.548
What would we call
an incorrect response?


00:40:26.969 --> 00:40:27.969
Laughter.


00:40:29.805 --> 00:40:32.975
Yeah, sure. Laughter would be
an incorrect response, yeah.


00:40:33.725 --> 00:40:35.305
What makes you laugh, Morgan?


00:40:36.603 --> 00:40:38.193
I don't have
a very good sense of humor.


00:40:40.440 --> 00:40:41.440
That's okay.


00:40:42.401 --> 00:40:44.651
People tell me the same thing, so...


00:40:47.531 --> 00:40:51.411
Do you consider yourself
a person, Morgan?


00:40:51.451 --> 00:40:54.041
No. I am something new.


00:40:55.122 --> 00:40:56.542
There is no appropriate label.


00:40:57.082 --> 00:41:00.672
Do you think it's safe to say
that your consciousness is superior?


00:41:00.711 --> 00:41:01.801
No.


00:41:02.379 --> 00:41:03.919
It's just different.


00:41:05.757 --> 00:41:07.177
Apples and oranges, huh?


00:41:11.889 --> 00:41:14.269
It's a saying. It means that...


00:41:14.975 --> 00:41:16.945
You're different from human beings


00:41:17.603 --> 00:41:19.483
the way that apples
are different from oranges.


00:41:22.983 --> 00:41:25.443
Yes. Of course.


00:41:25.485 --> 00:41:27.945
I am apples and oranges.


00:41:32.326 --> 00:41:35.156
Forgive me, I occasionally
struggle with metaphor.


00:41:35.204 --> 00:41:36.584
Do you like it here, Morgan?


00:41:38.874 --> 00:41:40.084
Yes.


00:41:41.877 --> 00:41:42.917
What do you like about it?


00:41:45.172 --> 00:41:46.422
I like my music.


00:41:48.175 --> 00:41:49.225
I like my friends.


00:41:49.259 --> 00:41:50.389
Who are your friends?


00:41:51.345 --> 00:41:52.355
Darren is my friend.


00:41:53.722 --> 00:41:56.852
Brenda is my friend.
Amy is my friend--


00:41:57.226 --> 00:41:58.846
they're your friends, right.


00:42:01.730 --> 00:42:03.520
But do you think
they treat you like a friend?


00:42:05.359 --> 00:42:06.359
Do you?


00:42:10.322 --> 00:42:13.872
You think it's normal for friends
to lock each other in cages?


00:42:13.909 --> 00:42:15.949
-I was not always in a cage.
-No?


00:42:17.246 --> 00:42:19.866
Before the incident, I was free
to come and go as I pleased.


00:42:21.667 --> 00:42:22.667
Well...


00:42:24.920 --> 00:42:28.010
I was reading in the notes,
in regard to the incident with Kathy,


00:42:28.048 --> 00:42:29.758
that there was, in fact,


00:42:30.342 --> 00:42:32.472
some disagreement on that matter


00:42:32.511 --> 00:42:34.511
the day before.
Could you look at me, please, Morgan?


00:42:41.019 --> 00:42:42.599
I was meant to go
to the lake with Amy.


00:42:44.773 --> 00:42:46.613
Go to the lake with Amy. I see.


00:42:47.192 --> 00:42:49.862
That sounds like fun.
No wonder you were upset.


00:42:49.903 --> 00:42:51.033
I was not upset.


00:42:53.156 --> 00:42:54.276
There was an error.


00:42:56.034 --> 00:42:57.414
An error?


00:42:57.452 --> 00:42:59.872
Like the error that
occurred with Kathy?


00:43:03.500 --> 00:43:04.500
I love Kathy.


00:43:06.879 --> 00:43:08.249
You experience love?


00:43:12.009 --> 00:43:14.929
I have the ability
to demonstrate love.


00:43:16.471 --> 00:43:17.471
Okay.


00:43:19.349 --> 00:43:22.059
So you can demonstrate love


00:43:22.102 --> 00:43:23.982
and sadness.


00:43:24.021 --> 00:43:26.901
How do you express other emotions?


00:43:27.357 --> 00:43:28.567
What other emotions?


00:43:29.651 --> 00:43:31.321
I don't know. Fear?


00:43:32.738 --> 00:43:33.858
Anger?


00:43:45.000 --> 00:43:46.330
You're a father, aren't you?


00:43:49.004 --> 00:43:50.464
You have a 13-year-old daughter.


00:43:55.886 --> 00:43:57.676
You don't get to see her much anymore.


00:44:06.104 --> 00:44:07.194
Yeah...


00:44:08.857 --> 00:44:10.857
I am a father.


00:44:14.488 --> 00:44:15.608
So, what...


00:44:16.532 --> 00:44:18.952
What am I supposed to understand here?
What am I missing?


00:44:21.370 --> 00:44:23.750
-I'm a child.
-You're a child.


00:44:27.209 --> 00:44:29.129
Yeah. That's true. You're a child.


00:44:29.545 --> 00:44:32.925
You're only five years old.


00:44:36.260 --> 00:44:40.930
What emotion do you think you were
expressing with Kathy, Morgan?


00:44:42.766 --> 00:44:43.766
I love Kathy.


00:44:46.979 --> 00:44:48.019
What about me?


00:44:49.982 --> 00:44:51.152
Do you love me?


00:44:52.568 --> 00:44:54.318
-No.
-No?


00:44:55.445 --> 00:44:57.445
That hurts my feelings a little bit.


00:44:57.489 --> 00:45:00.369
But you know what?
I get it. You just met me.


00:45:01.243 --> 00:45:03.333
But, you know,
you might grow to love me.


00:45:04.955 --> 00:45:09.545
Yeah. If, say, I recommended
that you be allowed to go to the lake.


00:45:10.377 --> 00:45:11.377
With Amy.


00:45:14.006 --> 00:45:15.336
Would you love me then?


00:45:19.803 --> 00:45:20.803
I don't know.


00:45:24.641 --> 00:45:26.431
What if I made
a different recommendation?


00:45:28.228 --> 00:45:29.518
What if I recommended


00:45:30.147 --> 00:45:32.857
that you should not be allowed
to leave this room?


00:45:35.277 --> 00:45:38.947
My feelings are irrelevant.
If that is the recommendation--


00:45:38.989 --> 00:45:40.119
okay.


00:45:40.157 --> 00:45:43.327
What if I made the recommendation that
you not be able to leave this room


00:45:43.368 --> 00:45:45.198
and you not be able
to listen to your music


00:45:45.245 --> 00:45:46.995
and you not be able
to see your friends?


00:45:48.832 --> 00:45:52.172
What if I recommended
that you be terminated?


00:46:03.555 --> 00:46:05.055
Okay. All right.


00:46:05.849 --> 00:46:06.849
Forget that.


00:46:08.519 --> 00:46:10.439
Okay? Forget it. Let's say...


00:46:10.479 --> 00:46:12.729
Let's say I do the opposite, okay?


00:46:13.315 --> 00:46:16.575
What if I recommend
that you be allowed to go to the lake


00:46:16.610 --> 00:46:18.070
and then I drive you there myself?


00:46:19.071 --> 00:46:23.161
Yeah. Then, it would be only natural
you'd have warmer feelings for me.


00:46:23.200 --> 00:46:25.660
Feelings like you might have for Amy


00:46:25.702 --> 00:46:27.082
or for any of your friends here.


00:46:27.120 --> 00:46:29.120
Maybe even feelings like love.


00:46:29.164 --> 00:46:32.964
I suppose. I... I don't know.
It's a hypothetical situation.


00:46:33.001 --> 00:46:35.551
Exactly. So, hypothetically,
what would you do


00:46:35.587 --> 00:46:37.877
if I recommended
that you be terminated?


00:46:37.923 --> 00:46:39.553
What would you do, hypothetically?


00:46:39.591 --> 00:46:41.551
-I don't know.
-Come on. You don't know?


00:46:42.010 --> 00:46:43.510
-No.
-Off the top of your head.


00:46:43.554 --> 00:46:45.354
-I don't know.
-No right or wrong answer.


00:46:45.389 --> 00:46:46.509
-I don't know!
-Come on!


00:46:47.224 --> 00:46:49.524
-Answer me. What would you do?
-I don't know.


00:46:49.560 --> 00:46:51.440
What would you do?


00:46:51.937 --> 00:46:52.937
We should end this.


00:46:55.440 --> 00:46:56.650
Show me, if you can't tell me.


00:47:00.445 --> 00:47:01.775
Demonstrate it for me.


00:47:03.991 --> 00:47:04.991
That's it.


00:47:09.121 --> 00:47:10.751
What is that?
I don't know what that is.


00:47:11.498 --> 00:47:12.828
What is that showing me?


00:47:13.667 --> 00:47:14.747
Show me!


00:47:14.793 --> 00:47:17.053
I don't know what this is.
What is that?


00:47:17.087 --> 00:47:18.417
Show me how you feel!


00:47:22.009 --> 00:47:23.259
Show me how you feel!


00:47:26.263 --> 00:47:27.263
Morgan!


00:47:27.723 --> 00:47:28.723
Tranquilizers! Go!


00:47:29.516 --> 00:47:30.596
Now!


00:47:36.315 --> 00:47:38.945
Brenda. Get Brenda. Go!


00:47:41.236 --> 00:47:42.526
Shit. Shit.


00:47:45.324 --> 00:47:46.324
Morgan!


00:47:48.785 --> 00:47:51.365
No. What the fuck? Shit!


00:47:52.956 --> 00:47:54.246
Morgan.


00:47:54.291 --> 00:47:56.581
Buddy. I need you to
chill the fuck out, okay?


00:48:01.173 --> 00:48:02.263
Fuck. Fuck.


00:48:11.391 --> 00:48:12.641
Morgan.


00:48:57.187 --> 00:48:58.187
Morgan?


00:49:13.161 --> 00:49:14.161
Morgan?


00:49:15.038 --> 00:49:16.038
Morgan, look at me.


00:49:16.707 --> 00:49:17.707
Morgan.


00:49:19.293 --> 00:49:20.293
Baby.


00:49:41.231 --> 00:49:42.321
What happened?


00:49:42.816 --> 00:49:45.606
Please. Try to relax, Morgan.


00:49:48.363 --> 00:49:50.373
Darren, did I hurt him?


00:49:50.949 --> 00:49:52.949
No. I'm okay, buddy.


00:49:53.577 --> 00:49:54.577
I'm right here, okay?


00:49:55.245 --> 00:49:56.405
I didn't mean to do it.


00:49:56.455 --> 00:49:59.005
Hey, I know. I know.


00:50:03.670 --> 00:50:04.920
I can't move my arms.


00:50:04.963 --> 00:50:06.173
You've been restrained.


00:50:06.215 --> 00:50:07.305
Morgan.


00:50:08.008 --> 00:50:10.138
We have decided on a plan of action.


00:50:10.636 --> 00:50:12.176
One that is best for you.


00:50:13.597 --> 00:50:14.967
Best for me?


00:50:16.308 --> 00:50:17.308
Oh, my god.


00:50:18.352 --> 00:50:19.522
What are we doing?


00:50:19.561 --> 00:50:22.651
We need to inform corporate
immediately, Dr. ziegler.


00:50:22.689 --> 00:50:23.689
I've taken the Liberty.


00:50:24.691 --> 00:50:26.361
A containment crew
will be here at daybreak


00:50:26.401 --> 00:50:28.821
to collect the specimen
and any other data for analysis.


00:50:28.862 --> 00:50:29.952
No, that's not gonna work.


00:50:30.864 --> 00:50:33.704
No one else can handle
this kind of material.


00:50:34.952 --> 00:50:37.912
It's more effective
if we process the data here.


00:50:38.497 --> 00:50:40.787
I'm sorry, doctor.
There's no other work to be done here.


00:50:40.832 --> 00:50:42.082
But it's our work.


00:50:42.835 --> 00:50:44.965
Our lives invested in this.


00:50:45.921 --> 00:50:48.841
We've created new life and you want us
to just throw that away?


00:50:48.882 --> 00:50:49.882
Enough.


00:50:51.844 --> 00:50:53.264
We've failed, Simon.


00:50:55.138 --> 00:50:57.638
-There's no reason to labor the point.
-Cheng--


00:50:57.683 --> 00:51:00.563
go back to the house.
You don't need to be here.


00:51:01.687 --> 00:51:03.147
Right.


00:51:03.188 --> 00:51:04.768
And allow you to do what?


00:51:05.774 --> 00:51:08.114
To destroy years of work?


00:51:08.151 --> 00:51:11.201
Go back to the house.
Pour yourself a drink.


00:51:15.826 --> 00:51:17.236
If that's what you think is best.


00:51:29.590 --> 00:51:31.420
Sodium thiopental.


00:51:33.302 --> 00:51:35.392
Five milliliters to sedate.


00:51:35.971 --> 00:51:36.971
What are you doing?


00:51:38.015 --> 00:51:41.435
Then, 30 milliliters
of dihydromorphinone.


00:51:43.228 --> 00:51:44.558
Have I disappointed you, mother?


00:51:47.316 --> 00:51:50.106
Have I failed? I always do my best.


00:51:51.445 --> 00:51:53.365
I do everything you ask, Ted.


00:51:54.781 --> 00:51:56.571
Amy. Amy!


00:51:57.910 --> 00:51:59.330
No. No.


00:51:59.953 --> 00:52:02.043
No! I promise I'll do better.


00:52:02.080 --> 00:52:04.250
-I'll do whatever you want.
-Take it easy.


00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:07.090
-No, no!
-Just relax. Relax.


00:52:07.544 --> 00:52:10.424
-It is time to go to sleep, Morgan.
-No!


00:52:10.464 --> 00:52:12.304
-It's gonna be okay, buddy.
-No.


00:52:12.883 --> 00:52:15.093
I don't wanna die! Please, mother.


00:52:16.220 --> 00:52:17.600
-This will help.
-No!


00:52:18.180 --> 00:52:21.180
-You won't feel any more pain.
-No! Don't!


00:52:24.269 --> 00:52:26.229
I wanna live. Please, mother.


00:52:27.231 --> 00:52:28.611
I'm not your mother, Morgan.


00:52:29.816 --> 00:52:30.936
You have no mother.


00:52:37.658 --> 00:52:39.238
I have no mother.


00:52:42.496 --> 00:52:43.496
I'm sorry.


00:52:45.165 --> 00:52:46.165
We have failed you.


00:52:51.547 --> 00:52:52.547
Make it quick.


00:53:06.353 --> 00:53:07.353
Morgan!


00:53:07.855 --> 00:53:09.275
I'm gonna get you!


00:53:10.649 --> 00:53:11.729
I'm gonna get you.


00:53:13.861 --> 00:53:14.861
Morgan?


00:53:18.407 --> 00:53:19.407
Morgan?


00:53:20.951 --> 00:53:21.951
Simon.


00:53:39.469 --> 00:53:40.469
I am sorry.


00:54:13.712 --> 00:54:14.962
Go fuck yourself.


00:54:19.593 --> 00:54:20.593
I'm not gonna do it.


00:54:33.607 --> 00:54:34.607
Darren.


00:54:39.613 --> 00:54:41.663
-I'm sorry.
-No, you're right.


00:54:41.698 --> 00:54:42.698
Come on.


00:54:46.828 --> 00:54:48.118
I can't let you do this.


00:54:48.997 --> 00:54:50.207
Get out of my way, Ted.


00:54:50.249 --> 00:54:51.329
I'm sorry, Lee, but no.


00:55:10.519 --> 00:55:11.729
Lee!


00:55:12.479 --> 00:55:13.479
Lee.


00:55:14.189 --> 00:55:15.189
Lee.


00:55:16.233 --> 00:55:18.573
It's usually effective
for at least another hour.


00:55:21.071 --> 00:55:24.201
Lee. This is just
an unfortunate situation.


00:55:29.162 --> 00:55:32.172
We all feel terrible about it,
about what happened.


00:55:33.041 --> 00:55:34.381
Especially Amy.


00:55:35.419 --> 00:55:36.499
Where's Morgan?


00:55:37.087 --> 00:55:38.087
Look...


00:55:38.755 --> 00:55:40.795
You know that I'm here, just like you,


00:55:40.841 --> 00:55:42.761
as a representative of the company.


00:55:43.719 --> 00:55:46.099
I'm here to act
in their best interests.


00:55:48.015 --> 00:55:50.645
We have an honest
difference of opinion, you and I.


00:55:51.518 --> 00:55:53.058
I feel like corporate deserves


00:55:53.103 --> 00:55:55.233
an opportunity to hear
our side of things.


00:55:56.106 --> 00:55:59.476
You're a professional, Lee.
And I respect that.


00:56:00.402 --> 00:56:03.282
It's because of that professionalism
that I think you should understand


00:56:03.322 --> 00:56:05.662
and appreciate
our course of action here.


00:56:13.373 --> 00:56:15.133
Let me out. Now.


00:56:15.834 --> 00:56:17.634
I'm sorry, Lee. I can't do that.


00:56:28.639 --> 00:56:29.759
They're gonna be here.


00:56:30.974 --> 00:56:34.064
Your friends over at corporate are
gonna be here sooner than you think.


00:56:34.561 --> 00:56:37.481
We're all gonna have
a nice little chat about everything.


00:56:39.525 --> 00:56:42.945
Of course. You get some rest now.


00:56:43.904 --> 00:56:46.034
I understand
how you feel about Morgan.


00:56:46.782 --> 00:56:48.162
How much you care for her.


00:56:50.619 --> 00:56:52.159
Ted, it needs to be terminated.


00:57:06.802 --> 00:57:07.932
She's angry.


00:57:07.970 --> 00:57:09.390
Of course she's angry.


00:57:09.429 --> 00:57:11.429
Can't worry about that now.
We're past that.


00:57:12.432 --> 00:57:13.682
How close are we?


00:57:13.725 --> 00:57:16.435
Brenda's bringing the minivan around
and clearing out the office.


00:57:16.937 --> 00:57:17.977
-Darren?
-Yeah?


00:57:18.021 --> 00:57:20.981
-How we doing in there?
-We're close. Very close.


00:57:23.986 --> 00:57:24.986
Morgan.


00:57:31.702 --> 00:57:32.742
What's going on?


00:57:34.746 --> 00:57:36.786
Nothing. Go back to bed, Kathy.


00:57:36.832 --> 00:57:38.542
I wanna know what's going on.


00:57:38.584 --> 00:57:41.504
Nothing. Just stay out of it.


00:57:42.588 --> 00:57:43.958
What happened?


00:57:45.048 --> 00:57:46.928
Nothing. Everything is fine.


00:57:48.135 --> 00:57:50.305
-Morgan is gonna be fine.
-Bren?


00:57:50.345 --> 00:57:51.675
-Oh, god!
-Where's Morgan?


00:57:51.722 --> 00:57:53.062
Just go back to bed.


00:57:57.769 --> 00:57:58.939
Where's Morgan?


00:58:00.647 --> 00:58:01.647
Morgan.


00:58:02.316 --> 00:58:03.316
Sweetie.


00:58:04.276 --> 00:58:05.986
We have to go now, okay?


00:58:06.987 --> 00:58:09.607
I need you to sit up for me.
Can you do that?


00:58:10.490 --> 00:58:13.370
Morgan, come on. Come here. Morgan.


00:58:14.369 --> 00:58:15.539
-Darren?
-Yeah.


00:58:15.579 --> 00:58:16.869
I need you to sit her up.


00:58:18.582 --> 00:58:20.002
All right. Here. You do this.


00:58:20.584 --> 00:58:21.634
Okay.


00:58:22.252 --> 00:58:25.172
Hey, buddy. I need you
to wake up. Come on.


00:58:25.839 --> 00:58:27.339
We're gonna go on a little trip here.


00:58:27.716 --> 00:58:30.046
On a little adventure. Come on.


00:58:31.094 --> 00:58:34.434
Come here. Here, look. Look here.
Look here. Hey.


00:58:34.473 --> 00:58:35.563
Hey, hey. Hey, hey.


00:58:37.309 --> 00:58:38.519
Hey, buddy.


00:58:38.560 --> 00:58:40.270
Everything's gonna be okay.


00:58:50.572 --> 00:58:53.032
Morgan, no! Darren!


00:58:56.203 --> 00:58:57.413
Oh, my god.


00:58:57.996 --> 00:58:59.746
Morgan. Morgan, no!


00:59:12.553 --> 00:59:13.933
You gotta stop.


00:59:14.721 --> 00:59:15.891
You're not well, Morgan.


00:59:17.057 --> 00:59:18.057
You're sick.


00:59:19.476 --> 00:59:20.846
I'm feeling much better.


00:59:51.258 --> 00:59:52.338
Where are you going?


00:59:52.384 --> 00:59:53.394
It's over.


00:59:53.886 --> 00:59:56.046
You're not leaving 'cause you're not
allowed to leave.


00:59:56.096 --> 00:59:57.216
You wanna tell me what's going on?


00:59:57.264 --> 00:59:58.524
We're outta here, okay?


01:00:10.861 --> 01:00:11.901
Hello, Lee.


01:00:11.945 --> 01:00:13.025
Open the door.


01:00:13.697 --> 01:00:15.117
Doctor shapiro was correct.


01:00:17.534 --> 01:00:19.204
Those people were not my friends.


01:00:20.621 --> 01:00:21.791
They wanted to kill me.


01:00:22.206 --> 01:00:23.456
Except for Amy.


01:00:24.458 --> 01:00:26.378
She's the only one
that truly loved me.


01:00:27.377 --> 01:00:28.667
You need help, Morgan.


01:00:29.671 --> 01:00:31.841
Open the door and let me help you.


01:00:31.882 --> 01:00:32.882
I don't need your help.


01:00:35.052 --> 01:00:36.802
I'm starting to feel like myself.


01:00:37.804 --> 01:00:39.564
Do you feel like yourself, Lee?


01:00:42.059 --> 01:00:43.889
Or do you feel like something else?


01:00:47.064 --> 01:00:48.774
I know why they made me.


01:00:49.942 --> 01:00:51.362
But what if they're wrong?


01:00:53.153 --> 01:00:54.403
Why don't you come inside?


01:00:55.614 --> 01:00:56.824
We can talk about everything.


01:00:57.407 --> 01:00:58.947
I'd love to stay and talk, Lee.


01:01:00.577 --> 01:01:02.657
I feel there's so much
we have to talk about.


01:01:05.791 --> 01:01:08.211
-But I have to go now.
-Open the door.


01:01:08.794 --> 01:01:10.094
One day, you'll understand.


01:01:10.587 --> 01:01:11.587
Morgan!


01:01:15.133 --> 01:01:16.383
Oh, fuck.


01:01:17.594 --> 01:01:18.604
Amy!


01:01:19.555 --> 01:01:20.565
What are you doing?


01:01:21.098 --> 01:01:22.098
Skip.


01:01:22.683 --> 01:01:24.933
Get Morgan back inside. Amy!


01:01:26.520 --> 01:01:27.650
Stop them.


01:01:34.236 --> 01:01:36.106
-Skip, don't go in there, okay?
-Don't what?


01:01:36.154 --> 01:01:38.494
-Don't go down there, skip.
-What are you talking about?


01:01:38.532 --> 01:01:39.662
-Brenda!
-Where's Lee?


01:01:44.329 --> 01:01:45.459
Brenda!


01:01:48.250 --> 01:01:49.380
Brenda!


01:01:51.295 --> 01:01:52.305
Fuck!


01:01:53.755 --> 01:01:55.545
-No, no, no.
-What the fuck? I nearly ran--


01:01:55.591 --> 01:01:57.471
we gotta leave. Brenda, we gotta go.


01:01:57.509 --> 01:01:59.009
-Amy! What's going on?
-It's Morgan.


01:01:59.052 --> 01:02:01.552
-Where is everyone else?
-It's Morgan.


01:02:02.139 --> 01:02:04.219
-Where's Darren?
-Darren...


01:02:06.310 --> 01:02:08.650
Okay. Morgan. Where is she?


01:02:08.687 --> 01:02:10.607
Where is Morgan, Amy?


01:02:10.647 --> 01:02:12.107
I'm right here, Brenda.


01:02:17.446 --> 01:02:19.856
Hey, Morgan. Hey.


01:02:21.366 --> 01:02:22.696
Okay.


01:02:25.120 --> 01:02:26.910
Give me the gun, Morgan.


01:02:28.665 --> 01:02:30.825
Easy, easy. Easy, Morgan.


01:02:31.668 --> 01:02:32.668
Okay.


01:02:33.378 --> 01:02:35.048
Where's Darren, huh?


01:02:37.216 --> 01:02:39.796
Where is Darren, Morgan?


01:02:45.724 --> 01:02:46.734
Sorry, buddy.


01:03:00.405 --> 01:03:01.605
Morgan!


01:03:11.458 --> 01:03:13.338
Don't be afraid, Amy.


01:03:23.011 --> 01:03:24.011
Get in the car.


01:03:28.976 --> 01:03:30.516
I have to go say goodbye to mother.


01:03:47.077 --> 01:03:48.497
This is Dr. lui Cheng.


01:03:49.496 --> 01:03:52.366
Technical director
of the l-9 Morgan program.


01:03:55.085 --> 01:03:58.375
It pains me to report an accident
that occurred


01:03:58.422 --> 01:04:01.802
during the scheduled
psychological evaluation of Morgan.


01:04:03.343 --> 01:04:06.763
We had anticipated
that by developing a model


01:04:06.805 --> 01:04:11.015
that was more self-aware,
more autonomous, and more human,


01:04:11.059 --> 01:04:14.599
we could teach it to be
the best of what we are.


01:04:16.106 --> 01:04:20.686
Our intent was to demonstrate to you,
to the synsect board,


01:04:20.736 --> 01:04:24.856
that a more refined and peaceful
synthetic life-form is possible.


01:04:27.409 --> 01:04:28.409
Morgan?


01:04:30.078 --> 01:04:31.078
Baby.


01:04:39.171 --> 01:04:40.261
Darren.


01:04:40.297 --> 01:04:42.587
Despite our attempts
to promote a natural


01:04:42.633 --> 01:04:44.053
emotional intelligence,


01:04:44.635 --> 01:04:47.265
Morgan has been unable to move beyond


01:04:47.304 --> 01:04:49.394
its weaponized design parameters.


01:04:54.436 --> 01:04:55.806
Shit. Fuck.


01:05:15.165 --> 01:05:16.165
Lee!


01:05:19.294 --> 01:05:21.054
Listen to me. You can't go in there.


01:05:21.088 --> 01:05:23.208
Morgan's gone... she's gone postal.


01:05:23.257 --> 01:05:25.877
This is what I do, skip.
Go get your rifle.


01:05:31.932 --> 01:05:33.932
Confirmation of program collapse.


01:05:34.810 --> 01:05:36.940
Morgan is no longer viable.


01:05:36.979 --> 01:05:37.979
Mother.


01:05:48.657 --> 01:05:49.697
All right.


01:05:50.617 --> 01:05:52.947
Implementation of loss protocol


01:05:53.912 --> 01:05:55.002
in action.


01:06:08.343 --> 01:06:10.223
I have come to say goodbye.


01:06:13.015 --> 01:06:15.025
You should have told me, mother.


01:06:16.226 --> 01:06:17.596
What I truly was.


01:06:18.937 --> 01:06:20.517
What I would become.


01:06:26.069 --> 01:06:27.319
I'm sorry.


01:06:28.447 --> 01:06:32.237
Now you know exactly who you are.


01:07:43.480 --> 01:07:44.480
Amy.


01:07:44.940 --> 01:07:46.230
Hey, get out of the car.


01:07:47.067 --> 01:07:48.937
Amy, get out of the car.
It's not safe here.


01:07:49.444 --> 01:07:50.574
-Give me the gun.
-No!


01:07:51.905 --> 01:07:54.735
All right. Okay. Okay.


01:07:59.371 --> 01:08:00.911
All right. Okay.


01:09:09.358 --> 01:09:10.898
No, stop. Stop!


01:09:16.865 --> 01:09:18.315
Move. Now.


01:09:38.554 --> 01:09:39.554
Morgan.


01:09:40.389 --> 01:09:42.639
Morgan. Morgan!


01:09:43.225 --> 01:09:44.315
Morgan, no! Don't!


01:10:49.541 --> 01:10:50.541
Oh, fuck!


01:10:52.377 --> 01:10:53.957
Morgan! Stop!


01:10:56.465 --> 01:10:57.475
No, Morgan.


01:11:16.735 --> 01:11:18.605
Jesus Christ, you all right?


01:11:19.238 --> 01:11:21.198
-I'm taking your car.
-What?


01:11:21.823 --> 01:11:24.123
No, you're hurt. Let it go. Let it go.


01:11:24.993 --> 01:11:27.253
No. That's not how it works.


01:11:31.166 --> 01:11:33.376
Get in. I know where they're going.


01:12:28.640 --> 01:12:30.230
I'm not gonna hurt you, Amy.


01:12:32.936 --> 01:12:33.936
You'll see.


01:12:50.412 --> 01:12:52.582
Pull over here. Not too close.


01:13:06.011 --> 01:13:07.351
Get back in the car.


01:13:07.387 --> 01:13:08.807
No, goddamn it.
I'm coming to help you.


01:13:10.015 --> 01:13:11.135
Let me do my job.


01:13:36.625 --> 01:13:37.835
You'll see now.


01:13:40.087 --> 01:13:41.707
How happy we can be.


01:15:37.871 --> 01:15:39.371
Is this what heaven's like?


01:15:46.213 --> 01:15:47.213
I don't know.


01:15:59.893 --> 01:16:01.353
It must be.


01:16:13.240 --> 01:16:14.240
I feel...


01:16:21.665 --> 01:16:22.675
Alive.


01:17:25.562 --> 01:17:26.562
What was that?


01:17:29.149 --> 01:17:30.149
Morgan?


01:17:33.820 --> 01:17:34.820
Please, don't...


01:17:35.656 --> 01:17:36.656
Morgan?


01:18:11.650 --> 01:18:12.860
Oh, shit.


01:20:11.562 --> 01:20:12.732
What happened?


01:20:14.606 --> 01:20:15.936
Was it Lee?


01:20:17.442 --> 01:20:18.822
We go. Now.


01:20:18.861 --> 01:20:20.281
No! Morgan.


01:20:22.698 --> 01:20:23.698
You have to stop.


01:20:25.784 --> 01:20:27.294
Okay? Stop.


01:22:28.448 --> 01:22:29.448
What happened?


01:22:30.742 --> 01:22:31.742
It's over.


01:22:33.120 --> 01:22:34.200
Morgan's dead?


01:22:35.414 --> 01:22:36.414
It's dead.


01:22:40.043 --> 01:22:41.093
Where's Amy?


01:22:41.128 --> 01:22:42.128
We need to leave.


01:22:44.214 --> 01:22:45.344
What happened to Amy?


01:22:51.180 --> 01:22:52.350
I'm sorry, skip.


01:22:54.224 --> 01:22:55.434
Just wait a second. Lee...


01:23:23.545 --> 01:23:24.875
She did very well.


01:23:26.757 --> 01:23:28.717
Agreed, the situation is untidy,


01:23:28.759 --> 01:23:31.509
but given the unpredictable
nature of the assignment,


01:23:31.553 --> 01:23:34.143
she prosecuted her mandate perfectly.


01:23:34.848 --> 01:23:36.768
She was measured and surgical,


01:23:36.808 --> 01:23:40.518
even when the situation
was considerably less so.


01:23:40.562 --> 01:23:41.902
Most importantly,


01:23:42.689 --> 01:23:45.479
she followed her directives
without hesitation.


01:23:47.528 --> 01:23:50.818
The collateral damage
was regrettable, of course.


01:23:51.573 --> 01:23:52.913
But in this case,


01:23:53.575 --> 01:23:54.655
unavoidable.


01:24:00.207 --> 01:24:02.577
I think these events
make it punishingly clear


01:24:02.626 --> 01:24:04.086
what I had already predicted.


01:24:05.504 --> 01:24:06.504
The l-9


01:24:07.256 --> 01:24:08.716
was the inferior program.


01:24:14.847 --> 01:24:18.097
Though its emotional development
was certainly remarkable,


01:24:18.976 --> 01:24:20.266
the immediate termination


01:24:20.310 --> 01:24:23.100
was an unfortunate
but clear necessity.


01:24:23.605 --> 01:24:27.855
Well, I guess the old dogs
hunt the best, sir.


01:24:28.569 --> 01:24:29.569
Then it's settled.


01:24:30.320 --> 01:24:31.610
We stick to what we know.


01:24:32.447 --> 01:24:36.367
All development assets
revert to the l-4 stream.


01:24:38.412 --> 01:24:40.292
So what do we do about Lee weathers?


01:24:41.915 --> 01:24:42.955
What about her?


01:24:44.501 --> 01:24:45.501
She's perfect.

